+indo-roman-trade | 1st century | Arikamedu | trade, movement | south | Indo-Roman trade relations; Arikamedu | Sea trade with Rome | Trade between the Indian subcontinent and the Roman Empire took the southern sea route by the Red Sea from around the beginning of the first century AD. Arikamedu, near Pondicherry, is an archaeological site of this period, excavated in the 1940s. | About 2,000 years ago ships sailed between India and the Roman Empire. Near Pondicherry, archaeologists have dug up an old port from that time.
